    given-names: "Sriram"

version: "0.1.0"

date-released: "2026-09-06"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Sriiraam/LongReadX-Long-Read-Structural-Variant-Analysis"

url: "https://github.com/Sriiraam/LongReadX-Long-Read-Structural-Variant-Analysis"

license: "MIT"

keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - genomics
  - long-read sequencing
  - PacBio HiFi
  - structural variants
  - Sniffles2
  - cuteSV
  - Truvari
  - Nextflow
  - workflow engineering
  - HG002
  - Genome in a Bottle

abstract: >
  LongReadX is a reproducible long-read structural-variant analysis workflow
  built around PacBio HiFi data from HG002. It performs long-read quality
  assessment, minimap2 alignment, BAM quality control, structural-variant
  calling with Sniffles2 and cuteSV, SV filtering, GIAB v5.0q benchmarking
  with Truvari, gene-overlap annotation using GENCODE, structured summary
  generation, SQLite storage, and interactive visualization through Streamlit.
